# Frames of the PDOs of the inverter at node 1, in the form of candump -L,
# which the build decodes by the description and compares with
# pdo_example.expected.
#
# TPDO1, the statuses in an MPDO, a status a frame, as this firmware sends
# them after it starts in the state of the bench below: the warning of
# params_defaulted and the critical can_vcu_connection_lost and ot_pwr, which
# TPDO4 of firmware 1a7c6f0 showed as flags beside a critical ot_motor, a
# status this inverter has not. The first frame is of the round, from 01h,
# the standing statuses follow as changes, and every fourth frame is of the
# round again.
can0 181#0100400100000000
can0 181#0100400401000000
can0 181#0100400F03000000
can0 181#0100401303000000
can0 181#0100400200000000
# The emergency, status 6, raised through 2202h, at severity 4, and cleared
# through 2201h.
can0 181#0100400704000000
can0 181#0100400700000000
# An object that the description does not name: 4000h:28, past the statuses.
can0 181#0100402800000000
# The TPDOs that adpt-etk-inverter, whose PDOs this inverter shares, sent at
# firmware 1a7c6f0 on can0 on 2026-10-07, in standby, with no VCU on the bus,
# as its workbench keeps them (inverter/test/test_pdo.cpp), on the COB-IDs of
# TPDO2 to TPDO4, on which this firmware sends them since the statuses took
# TPDO1. That firmware sent the angle in whole radians, 6 rad(el), and this
# one sends it in degrees, so the frame carries 344 °el. Its TPDO4, the
# status flags of a level, is gone.
can0 281#010A000000000003
can0 381#5401000000000002
can0 381#6001000000000001
can0 481#0000580100000002
